# Local modifications to the pinned tree, declared

The vendored tree is NOT pristine. It carries the instrumentation patch written for our
earlier experiment E-001:

  8 files changed, 92 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)
  plus one untracked file: crates/field/src/e001_count.rs

  crates/field/Cargo.toml
  crates/field/src/arch/aarch64/arithmetic/ghash.rs
  crates/field/src/lib.rs
  crates/hash/src/binary_merkle_tree.rs
  crates/ip-prover/Cargo.toml
  crates/ip-prover/src/fracaddcheck/mod.rs
  crates/ip-prover/src/sumcheck/drive.rs
  crates/ip-prover/src/sumcheck/mle_store.rs

The patch adds tracing spans and exact multiply/byte counters. The counters are behind the
`e001-count` Cargo feature, and **that feature is NOT enabled in any measurement in this
repository** — it adds an atomic increment per field multiply, which would make every timing
meaningless. With the feature off the patch is spans only.

# Harness

The measuring harness is a separate Cargo workspace, not part of binius64, and it lives in
this repository:

  scripts/binius64/harness

It depends on a clone of the revision above through path dependencies, supplied as
BINIUS64_ROOT; see that directory's README.md and setup.sh. Its release profile is declared
