src/bin/e006_negative.rs and src/bin/e006_verify_split.rs.

# Reproducing without the local patch

The patch described above is NOT required to reproduce E-006. The counters it adds are
behind the `e001-count` feature, the published harness manifest does not reference that
feature, and no E-006 measurement enabled it; with the feature off the patch is tracing
spans only, which no E-006 binary reads. A clean clone at the revision above is therefore
the intended starting point.

This was checked, not assumed. On 2026-08-24 the harness in this repository was built from
a fresh clone of THIS repository against a fresh `git clone` of binius64 checked out at the
revision above, with no patch applied:

  * the build succeeded on the pinned 1.97.1 toolchain;
  * the BUILD.md §2 build-integrity gate passed at ratio 0.985, inside the 0.983-0.996
    band the campaign recorded;
  * `scripts/run-negative.sh t1-0` reproduced `data/negative/t1-0/report.txt`
    byte for byte, including every witness word and the 345,536-byte proof size;
  * `scripts/run-cell.sh t1-0:1:1` reproduced every structural quantity of
    `data/cells/t1-0-r1-t1/cell.json` exactly - 65,536 IMUL, 65,280 AND, 8,192 zero
    constraints, 345,536 proof bytes - with prove and verify medians 5-6% above the
    published run, which is the drift a non-dedicated machine produces (see BUILD.md §4).

Timing figures are therefore machine-dependent, as declared; the circuits, the proof sizes
and the correctness verdict are not, and they reproduce exactly from a clean clone.

