# Second local modification, declared (2026-09-03, gate G-13a)

`count-muls`: a Cargo feature in `crates/field` (new `src/mul_class_count.rs`, plus one
counter call at each `wide_mul`/`square` choke point of the GHASH arithmetic) that counts
field multiplications by operand class. OFF by default; when off, the feature adds no symbol
and no static to the binary (`nm` clean), so every timing figure in this benchmark is taken
from a tree whose generated code is unchanged. Patch: `experiments/E-001-cost-kernel-split/
scripts/patches/binius64-e001-instrumentation-plus-count-muls.patch` — the CUMULATIVE diff of
the vendored tree against the pinned commit (17 files: the E-001 span instrumentation above plus
this feature); apply it alone to reproduce the tree. Result: `experiments/E-001-cost-kernel-split/
RESULTS-G13a.md`.
